Fonology's R code and original documentation are licensed under the MIT
License stated in DESCRIPTION and LICENSE.

The following data components have separate licenses:

* data/fr_lex.rda is adapted from Lexique 4, distributed through
  OpenLexicon under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
  International License (CC BY-SA 4.0):
  https://lexique.org/databases/Lexique400/README-Lexique.txt

* data/sp_lex.rda and data/it_lex.rda are adapted from English Wiktionary
  data extracted by Wiktextract and distributed by Kaikki. They are licensed
  under CC BY-SA 4.0. The adaptations select language and dialect variants,
  normalize IPA symbols, and add package syllabification where documented:
  https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Wiktionary:Copyrights
  https://kaikki.org

* data/pt_lex_fix.rda combines original maintainer corrections with a curated
  set of Portuguese stress and vowel-quality corrections adapted from English
  Wiktionary data extracted by Wiktextract/Kaikki. The combined dataset is
  distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0. The adaptation retains only unambiguous
  general-Brazil pronunciation facts, converts them to diacritized Portuguese
  forms, and derives broad IPA through Fonology's Portuguese pipeline.

Copyright in Wiktionary material belongs to the individual Wiktionary
contributors. Attribution is provided through the source and history pages at
https://en.wiktionary.org. Wiktionary-derived data were modified as described
above; neither the Wikimedia Foundation, Wiktionary contributors, Wiktextract,
nor Kaikki endorses Fonology.

